Splash WebGL vortex (frontend/components/common/splash/singularity-renderer.ts):

STX ships an original polar-spiral accretion-disk fragment shader under Apache-2.0.

A prior draft considered porting "Singularity" by @XorDev on ShaderToy
(https://www.shadertoy.com/view/3csSWB), as also embedded by Inspira UI's
Singularity Background. Findings:

- The ShaderToy source comment does not grant MIT/Apache; Inspira's MIT license
  covers its Vue wrapper only and does not relicense the embedded GLSL.
- ShaderToy's default when no license is pasted in the shader is
  Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 (CC BY-NC-SA 3.0),
  which is incompatible with Apache-2.0 commercial redistribution of this product.
- Independent redistributions of the same algorithm (e.g. AppKade/singularity)
  likewise label the shader CC BY-NC-SA 3.0.

Therefore that third-party algorithm is not retained. Do not reintroduce it
under a forged Apache/ASF header.
